# `power::OpfOptions`

Iteration budget and tolerances of the optimal power flow.

## Signature

```cpp
power::OpfOptions
```

## What It Does

Controls for `opf`.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `max_iterations` | The iteration budget of the sequential quadratic-programming method. | 160 |
| `constraint_tolerance` | The largest violation of the network equations and limits accepted at convergence. | 1e-8 |
| `optimality_tolerance` | The first-order optimality accepted at convergence. | 1e-8 |

## Returns

A value; validated by `opf`.

## Errors

A non-positive tolerance or a budget below one is rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

Loose tolerances stop sooner at lower accuracy. A budget that is too small returns `converged` false with a message naming the measure that was still too large.

